    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d336">

                <pb facs="0602" n="474" xml:id="pg474"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72113 Au 7/27</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Alien Property Custodian</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sutherland</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi><anchor n="20" xml:id="d336-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-23"><hi rendition="#italic">May 23,
                        1928</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to reply to your letter of
                    May 21,<anchor n="21" xml:id="d336-f2"/> in which you enclosed a copy of a
                    communication from the Minister of Austria.<anchor n="22" xml:id="d336-f3"/></p>
                <p>The Minister desires to know what will become of property seized as belonging to
                    Austrian citizens if no claim is filed within a year or if proof is not
                    submitted as to ownership, as provided in the Settlement of War Claims Act of
                    1928, and he asks whether or not it would be credited to the Austrian Government
                    under Section 7, of the said Act.</p>
                <p>You are advised that it is the view of this office that there is no law
                    authorizing the transfer of said sums. Subsection (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >g</hi>) of Section 25<anchor n="23" xml:id="d336-f4"/> is specific as to
                    what sums should be transferred to this account and it mentions none other than
                    Austrian property or that of a corporation in which all of the stock is owned by
                    the Austrian Government.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Howard Sutherland</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d336-f1" n="20" type="source" xml:id="d336-f1-content">
                <p>On June 15, the Secretary of State transmitted a copy of this communication to
                    the Austrian Minister (file No. 763.72113 Au 7/31).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d336-f2" n="21" xml:id="d336-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d336-f3" n="22" xml:id="d336-f3-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg472">p. 472</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d336-f4" n="23" xml:id="d336-f4-content">
                <p>See sec. 10, 45 Stat. 269, for revised sec. 25.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
